"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"1d499f10-c496-4248-9786-fcb81b5c2103\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"1d499f10-c496-4248-9786-fcb81b5c2103\"\u003e Alaska needed a woman from the outside to help them get their heads out of their asses? \u003c/label\u003e. Yes. Like the first book, did the author add in random sort of important things about the characters 75% into the book? Yes. (\u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"dfaf0b24-ab26-4900-844c-1cd62e6e264e\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"dfaf0b24-ab26-4900-844c-1cd62e6e264e\"\u003e I'm looking at you, Landen's side job, and I'm looking at you Super-Important-Willow-Tree \u003c/label\u003e) Did I wish there was more explanation into how the Royal States became the way that they are, in which a well educated, independent woman believes that the only way to have children is by getting married? You betcha.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI have questions about the Royal States' university system and treatment of females in academia, but I will be a good reader and tell myself that during the upheaval between USA and RSA, a field that was majority female reverted back to being mostly male because all the ladies were too busy getting married and having children and except for Summer, largely stopped caring about pursuing their academic degrees in archaeology.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eKudos to the author, she did definitely do research into the Mesoamerican societies that were described, although it really worried me that someone like Simon could get a doctorate and still not know how to read the language of the culture he focused on. Also why didn't everyone spend all their time in labs trying to piece together pottery sherds or writing endless reports and papers on their findings? Usually you just get 1000000 bug bites and find like, two pots and maybe an old hoe (takes deep breath, reminds self that actual archaeology is too boring to make a good novel and that earthweaving allows people to find the cool stuff with little to no hassle, lets out breath) \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"caef998e-eeeb-4b96-9ff7-d2a41bd8a92a\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"caef998e-eeeb-4b96-9ff7-d2a41bd8a92a\"\u003eEqually upsetting, why weren't more academics FLIPPING THEIR SH*T about the temples discovered outside of Mexico? ALSO what the heck happened to that society that they crumbled so quickly and without any other traces? Like, that giant city, let's talk about that. I have SO MANY questions and although I'm pretty sure the author won't be exploring this fascinating blend of three cultures erecting giant temples and cities thousands of miles away in any of her later books, I WANNA KNOW WHAT THEY WERE DOING THERE hahahahaha \u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI liked that there were less adult tantrums in this book, that was nice. I did like Summer and Landen as a couple, and wish that there was actually more page-time devoted to exploring their relationship. Instalove always weirds me out, and I'm pretty sure they'd spent less than 12 hours being able to have coherent conversations with each other before Landen \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"06b7a3c5-34fa-4baf-a6b8-a79e0c733500\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"06b7a3c5-34fa-4baf-a6b8-a79e0c733500\"\u003e made her marry him while she was drugged. Also, that sounds illegal, even if they loved each other. \u003c/label\u003e. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eUmmm I'm making it sound like I hated this book, but I really didn't. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e3.75/5 stars","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A11KWLCO5FXR5P\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:7589274":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":7589274,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1329068126i/7589274._UY200_CR52,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":13,"textReviewsCount":2872,"name":"Katherine","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/7589274-katherine","contributor":null,"id":7589274},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1MYDJDK9XG6O2":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1MYDJDK9XG6O2"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1MYDJDK9XG6O2\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1MYDJDK9XG6O2","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1MYDJDK9XG6O2"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/7589274?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2294049110"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.nUp5_ljN6zIHAYR0BOV6pw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.nUp5_ljN6zIHAYR0BOV6pw","creator":{"__ref":"User:7589274"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1520877385877,"createdAt":1520876777940,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1520877385241,"text":"\u003cstrong\u003eDifficult to get into but satisfying to finish\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI had a fair amount of difficulty getting into this book. It really came down to the protagonist. Summer is bold, snarky, and refuses to take any crap. But atthe the beginning I found her almost too abrasive. She was cynical about all royals and all men, and even when she met a guy she liked it didn't show. Her interactions with Landen were all about tests, and waiting for him to mess up. From that I didn't really get the feeling she was into him, but as soon as the magic starts all she talks about is finding Landen and marrying him. Between how she had acted and how she was saying she felt, I was having a lot of difficulty buying the romantic connection, so it took a bit more story before I could really settle in and enjoy it.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs we learn more about Summer it becomes more obvious why she acts so harsh to the outside world. Between her education, her thesis, her power, and the men she worked with, she had a long history of all bad with no good, no matter how hard you worked. She was cynical as she looked to a future of more of the same. The magic that happens in the book make a life crazy, but it also gives her a chance to see a future that could be different than what she ever imagined. Between the magical trials and the people standing in her way to stop her, that future isn't easy to get to, but all the hard work she's done her whole life make her unafraid to fight. By the end Summer has a new future, and finally has happiness, which makes it all worth the troubles before.","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1MYDJDK9XG6O2\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:12854357":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":12854357,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1776789030i/12854357._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":57,"textReviewsCount":1245,"name":"Diane","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/12854357-diane","contributor":null,"id":12854357},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/12854357?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/2757978273"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.P0CnxUvruguzN0rST-bUAQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.P0CnxUvruguzN0rST-bUAQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:12854357"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1553216009984,"createdAt":1553210682244,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1553216009363,"text":"\u003cstrong\u003e4.33 GR stars: archaeology (archaeolinguistics, even!), magic, misadventure, a heroine who takes no guff, a lovable royal hero, ... What's not to love? \u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis may be my favorite R.J. Blain story so far (though I've still got a bunch to catch up on). \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI loved the conversations (including arguments), and how she worried about being a queen when she's a \"queen b****\" (though her first major act in his realm was to put right a long-standing grievous wrong — trigger warning only needed if even general mention of past sexual assault spoils a mainly light story for you). \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI loved the twists on the tribal history and mythology of Mexico et al. The unpredictable leaps the relics and ruins lead to provide a fun mix of challenging settings.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eA few past Royal States characters show up, without its feeling forced.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI only made eight nitpicky notes in the book (not counting the highlighted lines to be *savored*!), for a couple goofs that look like rewording remnants, a couple duplicated word-choices that can be avoided, a couple instances of a regional [mis]use of the past participle (instead of the present participle, e.g., \"Do you need rescued?\" ) that I hate nearly as much as \"I could care less\" but probably shouldn't call errors, and a couple other minor proofreading slips.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI think I'm going to read another Royal States romance now. See ya!","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/AJC2WML80OK0I\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.uz1jxOur_-iDqAPQTE19zA\"}}"},"likeCount":0,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":0},"User:40536102":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":40536102,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1503751883i/40536102._UX200_CR0,100,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":3,"textReviewsCount":15,"name":"Momo Chan","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/40536102-momo-chan","contributor":null,"id":40536102},"User:kca://p